# PHY-019 — compatible coarse-graining with retained memory

**Scientific status: PASS_PROJECTIVE_MAPS_WITH_EXACT_MEMORY; naive Markov closure refuted.**

## Exact projective representation maps

For nested pair/block averages on an eight-cell cycle,

`B_(4->2) B_(8->4) = B_(8->2)`

exactly. Thus the coarse **representation** can be coassociative without fitting independent coefficients at every level.

That does not make the coarse **dynamics** Markovian. For the controlled linear relaxation

`dot z = -(a I + kappa L_C8) z`, with `a=0.5`, `kappa=1`,

an orthogonal Haar split into four pair averages `c` and four pair differences `f` gives blocks `A_cc,A_cf,A_ff`. The eliminated block has gap `gamma=2.5` and `||A_cf||=1`.

Eliminating `f` exactly gives

`dot c(t) = -A_cc c(t) - A_cf exp(-A_ff t) f(0) + integral_0^t K(t-s)c(s) ds`,

with

`K(t)=A_cf exp(-A_ff t) A_fc`.

The memory is nonzero. Its L1 operator norm is bounded by `||A_cf||^2/gamma = 0.4`.

## Naive closure fails

Using the same unit-coefficient cycle generator on four coarse cells does not commute with averaging: the generator closure defect has operator norm about `1.4142`.

The zero-frequency Schur/adiabatic generator is

```text
[[ 1.3571429, -0.5      ,  0.1428571, -0.5      ],
 [-0.5      ,  1.3571429, -0.5      ,  0.1428571],
 [ 0.1428571, -0.5      ,  1.3571429, -0.5      ],
 [-0.5      ,  0.1428571, -0.5      ,  1.3571429]]
```

so eliminating subcell variables generates a next-neighbor term of magnitude `1/7`, even though the fine law was nearest-neighbor.

## Controlled low-frequency approximation

The exact frequency-dependent generator is

`A_eff(s)=A_cc-A_cf(sI+A_ff)^(-1)A_fc`.

For `|s|<gamma`,

`||A_eff(s)-A_eff(0)|| <= ||A_cf||^2 |s|/[gamma(gamma-|s|)]`.

Thus a Markov approximation is controlled only when observation frequencies are small relative to the eliminated gap. There is no license to discard memory at arbitrary scales.

## FIN interpretation

PHY-008's growing causal-ball memory was not an implementation accident. PHY-019 supplies an exact analytic control showing the same general mechanism: projective observables may compose exactly while eliminated dynamics acquires memory and longer-range effective couplings.

This is not yet a nonlinear FIN continuum theorem. It is the required warning/bridge template for one: any later elimination of hard FIN modes must pay the gap and nonlinear remainder rather than silently replacing the effective process by a local Markov law.
